WEBVTT

00:11.910 --> 00:18.210
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

01:29.990 --> 01:34.490
#40: EMBRACING YOUR AMBITIONS
IN THE LIGHT PART 5

01:35.910 --> 01:39.250
Mr. Sunraku is getting chewed up!

01:39.250 --> 01:41.830
I am not a candy!

01:41.830 --> 01:44.510
Will this dispel his curse?

01:45.210 --> 01:47.460
Shouldn't we help him or something?

01:47.460 --> 01:49.460
Mr. Sunraku...

01:52.220 --> 01:54.680
A-Are you okay, Mr. Sunraku?!

01:56.140 --> 01:59.180
I feel like chewing gum
spat out on the street...

02:00.350 --> 02:03.480
But now I'm finally free
of this godforsaken Mark...

02:05.230 --> 02:07.730
What?!

02:07.730 --> 02:12.610
Not only does it not disappear,
but its presence has only gotten stronger!

02:12.610 --> 02:14.700
"Lycagon's Contusion."

02:14.700 --> 02:19.790
"The Night Emperor no longer sees those
who defeat her incarnation as mere prey."

02:19.790 --> 02:23.120
"That is the sign of an acknowledged
"enemy" worthy to defeat,"

02:23.120 --> 02:26.040
and the engraving of a strong hero
recognized by a Colossus."

02:26.580 --> 02:29.420
"The Mark etched onto the soul
can only be removed

02:29.420 --> 02:32.250
by defeating the true form
of the black wolf."

02:34.090 --> 02:38.600
Hey! Not only did it not get removed,
but it's even stronger now!

02:39.140 --> 02:42.850
Now I can't remove it
unless I defeat the real one!

02:43.600 --> 02:46.100
It's gotten a lot darker now.

02:46.810 --> 02:50.610
That means not even
the Saint Eristella can remove it?

02:50.610 --> 02:53.190
As for the effects...

02:53.780 --> 02:57.450
It makes me targeted more
often by high-level monsters...

02:57.800 --> 03:02.750
Oh? I can equip stuff on
the contused body parts?!

03:02.750 --> 03:06.460
Oh, sweet! So I can equip gear after all!

03:06.460 --> 03:09.210
Now that changes a lot of things!

03:10.670 --> 03:16.130
"However, items equipped on the contused parts
will break after a set period of time."

03:17.010 --> 03:21.390
Break... after a set period of time?

03:21.390 --> 03:23.140
Are you kidding me?!

03:23.140 --> 03:25.980
Stripping me off ain't
gonna make anyone happy!

03:25.980 --> 03:28.730
What the hell are you
putting on me, you cur!

03:28.730 --> 03:31.460
Take it back right now!
I demand a return!

03:32.690 --> 03:33.900
Hey?!

03:34.320 --> 03:36.530
What?! Wait!

03:36.530 --> 03:41.030
Don't give me that "My job here is done"
look and disappear!

03:45.160 --> 03:46.840
Oh my god...

03:47.870 --> 03:50.250
I never thought this would happen...

03:50.250 --> 03:52.460
C-Cheer up, okay?

03:52.460 --> 03:55.550
Running at full speed
should put your mind off it!

03:56.340 --> 03:57.050
I'll keep that to RTAs, thanks.

03:57.050 --> 03:58.180
RTA=SPEEDRUNNING
I'll keep that to RTAs, thanks.

03:58.180 --> 03:59.430
COMPETING ON THE FASTEST CLEAR TIME
I'll keep that to RTAs, thanks.

03:59.430 --> 04:01.850
U-Um, Sunraku.

04:01.850 --> 04:03.850
Sorry to interrupt you while you're down.

04:04.810 --> 04:05.600
Yes?

04:06.100 --> 04:10.810
This "EX Unique Scenario" is mentioned
in the results screen. Could it be...

04:11.400 --> 04:12.610
Oh, right.

04:12.610 --> 04:13.150
EX UNIQUE SCENARIO
Oh, right.

04:13.150 --> 04:13.900
EX UNIQUE SCENARIO

04:13.900 --> 04:16.240
"THE TORCH OF COURAGE THAT BANISH
This is the scenario meant to finish

04:16.240 --> 04:18.110
THE DARKNESS OF NIGHT" - BEGIN? NO, YES
things off with a Unique Monster.

04:18.610 --> 04:21.320
It was the same deal with
Wethermon the Tombguard.

04:21.320 --> 04:23.990
I don't really get it,

04:23.990 --> 04:28.330
but is it okay for me to take on
this EX Unique Scenario?

04:28.730 --> 04:31.920
Why not? It'll be a lot of fun for you.

04:31.920 --> 04:34.500
You two helped me a lot, too.

04:35.340 --> 04:40.220
No point trying to monopolize
these scenarios now.

04:40.220 --> 04:44.240
I'll have Pencilgon think about
how we'll work this all out.

04:44.970 --> 04:49.810
Come to think of it, apart from the title,
there was one other reward, wasn't it?

04:49.810 --> 04:51.520
Let's see...

04:51.520 --> 04:54.900
UNIQUE CONDITION - GUIDING TORCH
"Unique Condition: Guiding Torch."

04:54.900 --> 04:57.490
UNIQUE CONDITION - GUIDING TORCH
"When Lycagon the Nightslayer

04:57.490 --> 04:59.070
UNIQUE CONDITION - GUIDING TORCH
is within a certain distance,"

04:59.070 --> 05:01.280
UNIQUE CONDITION - GUIDING TORCH
"it will point in her direction."

05:01.670 --> 05:03.200
I see.

05:03.200 --> 05:06.870
With this thing, it's possible
to find the real deal.

05:06.870 --> 05:09.040
In other words, a radar.

05:09.490 --> 05:12.170
I only ran to her today
by pure coincidence,

05:12.170 --> 05:15.800
and not because I accepted
an EX Unique Scenario or anything.

05:16.380 --> 05:18.760
She got a leg up on me this time,

05:18.760 --> 05:22.760
but next time I'll be sure to bring
my passport and stride right in.

05:24.060 --> 05:26.620
I don't know where she's
shutting herself away right now,

05:27.100 --> 05:30.640
but I'll search for her to the ends
of the land, the sky, and the sea,

05:30.640 --> 05:33.020
and drag her out into the light for sure.

05:34.110 --> 05:37.570
Go ahead and act all breezy
while you still can,

05:37.570 --> 05:39.530
Lycagon the Nightslayer!

05:40.990 --> 05:43.200
I know you can do it!

05:43.200 --> 05:43.990
You bet!

05:43.990 --> 05:45.990
Yes! I'm sure you can beat her!

05:47.660 --> 05:51.120
Akitsuakane, Ceecrue, and Emul,

05:51.120 --> 05:53.620
and especially Rei,
you were a great help.

05:55.460 --> 05:59.300
You helped me not only to beat this area
but also to fend off Lycagon.

05:59.300 --> 06:02.260
O-Oh, no worries! Don't mind it!

06:02.260 --> 06:04.450
I'll go out with you
anytime you need—

06:04.450 --> 06:07.260
Go... Go... out!

06:07.260 --> 06:09.830
Go out... G-Go...

06:11.730 --> 06:12.470
Huh?

06:13.020 --> 06:14.730
Oh, also,

06:14.730 --> 06:18.520
I nearly forgot because of that fierce fight,
but we're here to beat this area.

06:18.520 --> 06:20.900
We gotta find and beat the Area Boss.

06:20.900 --> 06:24.030
A boss raid? Let us join you!

06:24.450 --> 06:25.950
Right, Ceecrue?

06:25.950 --> 06:26.950
Verily.

06:26.950 --> 06:29.120
Glad to hear that.

06:29.120 --> 06:32.120
Rei, what kinda boss is in this area?

06:33.460 --> 06:34.940
U-Umm, right.

06:36.750 --> 06:40.250
The Area Boss of this
Lightless Barrens

06:40.250 --> 06:42.670
is a Wyvern whose scales
give it camouflage.

06:43.260 --> 06:46.010
It flies into the air
when the battle starts

06:46.010 --> 06:48.680
and almost never goes back
to the ground.

06:48.680 --> 06:50.680
It flies around...

06:51.310 --> 06:55.140
I've struggled against
monsters like that.

06:56.900 --> 06:59.070
But this time I got Emul and you guys.

06:59.070 --> 07:00.940
We could work things out
with some magic.

07:00.940 --> 07:05.400
But this Area Boss has
a certain tricky characteristic.

07:05.400 --> 07:10.950
It can take control of our magic
and even steal our weapons.

07:10.950 --> 07:11.700
What?!

07:11.700 --> 07:13.790
So we can't use our magic?!

07:13.790 --> 07:17.750
We were just fighting Lycagon,
so I guess this won't be an easy fight.

07:18.210 --> 07:19.790
Better keep our guards up!

07:19.790 --> 07:21.800
Psyche ourselves up, we shall.

07:32.890 --> 07:34.060
So that is...

07:34.060 --> 07:35.480
...the Area Boss!

07:35.480 --> 07:36.520
Yes.

07:36.520 --> 07:38.020
The "taker."

07:38.020 --> 07:40.820
Based on that, this Area Boss
was given the name...

07:40.820 --> 07:42.690
Usurper Dragon.

07:46.280 --> 07:49.120
AREA BOSS
USURPER DRAGON

07:49.910 --> 07:53.450
Heh, I've got somewhere to be in time.

07:54.870 --> 07:59.210
Sorry, but we'll end this quick,
Usurper Dragon!

08:01.920 --> 08:06.130
Our fight has only just begun!

08:07.430 --> 08:09.930
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:10.930 --> 08:13.720
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:13.720 --> 08:15.350
Whoa, so bright.

08:15.350 --> 08:17.940
What a beautiful sunrise.

08:17.940 --> 08:20.900
I suppose the time must
have caught up with us.

08:20.900 --> 08:23.610
It did take a while, yeah.

08:25.650 --> 08:28.030
Oh, you're up.

08:28.030 --> 08:30.490
Fweh?! Where are we?!

08:30.490 --> 08:32.990
What happened to me?!

08:33.370 --> 08:36.250
What happened to the Usurper Dragon?

08:36.250 --> 08:40.080
Man, Usurper Dragon was a menace.

08:40.080 --> 08:40.750
Huh?

08:40.750 --> 08:45.380
It soars the sky, thieving our weapons.
It was quite the travesty.

08:45.380 --> 08:46.760
Huh? What?

08:46.760 --> 08:50.010
But you did such a great job
in that situation, Emul.

08:53.890 --> 08:58.020
What did I do?
I don't remember anything.

08:58.020 --> 09:01.520
I could never have the guts
to try something that dangerous.

09:01.520 --> 09:02.810
Dangerous?!

09:02.810 --> 09:06.190
I'm sorry. All because of my debuff,

09:06.190 --> 09:09.860
we wouldn't have had to expose
Emul to so much danger.

09:10.210 --> 09:12.360
Danger?!

09:12.820 --> 09:14.240
We had no other choice.

09:14.240 --> 09:16.410
That's the rebound
of Armageddon, right?

09:16.410 --> 09:19.750
It's pretty nasty having all your stats
halved for a whole day.

09:20.250 --> 09:23.500
But you're still stronger than me, though!

09:23.500 --> 09:24.420
No, of course not.

09:24.420 --> 09:28.090
What danger? What really happened?

09:28.090 --> 09:31.090
There, there. I had your recovery
under consideration, too.

09:31.090 --> 09:33.720
It's just that things
went a little off the rails,

09:33.720 --> 09:36.680
and you nearly got eaten and dropped
from the sky many times.

09:36.680 --> 09:38.010
I got eaten?!

09:38.010 --> 09:38.880
Man, lay off.

09:39.520 --> 09:41.940
Well, I suppose you're
better off not knowing.

09:41.940 --> 09:42.900
You sure?!

09:43.480 --> 09:48.400
Speaking of rebounds,
my Gilta Brille broke and I can't use it.

09:48.400 --> 09:50.910
If we didn't come up
with that "Super Emul Cannon,"

09:50.910 --> 09:52.320
we could've had a worse time.

09:52.320 --> 09:55.410
What's this "Super Emul Cannon"?

09:55.410 --> 09:56.200
This is all news to me!

09:56.200 --> 09:57.160
SUPER EMUL CANNON: RABBIT CANNON
This is all news to me!

09:57.160 --> 09:59.700
SUPER EMUL CANNON: RABBIT CANNON
It definitely involves me, doesn't it?!

09:59.700 --> 10:05.460
As thy older brother, I am proud
to see thy Vorpal Soul shine through.

10:06.460 --> 10:09.550
Somebody please just explain to me
what happened already!

10:09.550 --> 10:10.710
Mr. Sunraku!

10:11.050 --> 10:15.640
Well, it was not all that important
a fight compared to Lycagon's.

10:15.640 --> 10:18.010
It's not that big of a deal
you can't recall it.

10:18.010 --> 10:20.140
That's not the point!

10:20.140 --> 10:21.480
Hmph!

10:21.480 --> 10:25.320
C'mon, cheer up, will you?
I'll buy you a carrot later.

10:25.320 --> 10:27.730
I'll think about it if you throw in
a mana potion too.

10:27.730 --> 10:28.980
Sure thing.

10:28.980 --> 10:31.740
As we all having this talk,
it is now in sight.

10:32.150 --> 10:33.950
Oh, so that's it?

10:33.950 --> 10:35.160
Yes.

10:35.160 --> 10:40.740
This was the final accessible town
before this Summer's massive update.

10:40.740 --> 10:44.040
Now it's a port town
leading to the new continent,

10:44.040 --> 10:48.290
a second "departure" town
lots of players flock to.

10:48.290 --> 10:49.420
Fifticia.

10:49.420 --> 10:51.630
FIFTEENTH TOWN - FIFTICIA

10:51.630 --> 10:54.520
Just as you would expect from
the final town of the continent.

10:54.520 --> 10:56.550
It has plenty of fancy buildings.

10:56.550 --> 10:57.510
Sure is!

10:57.930 --> 11:00.310
So you put on a mask inside the town, huh?

11:00.310 --> 11:01.140
Huh?

11:01.140 --> 11:04.480
Is it to hide the Mark
Siegwurm put on you?

11:04.480 --> 11:06.730
Yeah, right.

11:06.730 --> 11:08.730
When I'm in a place with lots of people.

11:12.530 --> 11:18.490
I can't exactly tell him that I accidentally
based my avatar's face on my real one.

11:18.490 --> 11:22.120
You wore a white cloth before, didn't you?

11:22.490 --> 11:25.120
It's hard to move in that.

11:25.590 --> 11:30.090
Oh, yeah, how can you wear a mask
when the Mark is on your face?

11:30.090 --> 11:33.590
This counts as an accessory,
not a headgear.

11:33.590 --> 11:34.800
Oh?

11:34.800 --> 11:38.930
Mr. Sunraku! Mr. Sunraku!
They sell lots of grimoire in here!

11:38.930 --> 11:40.760
Maybe we can dig up some treasures!

11:40.760 --> 11:44.430
Didn't I just buy you a ton of
carrots and magic potions?

11:46.060 --> 11:48.600
We still have a lot of things to do.

11:49.150 --> 11:53.070
Let's see... It's around five
in the morning, right?

11:53.070 --> 11:55.110
The meet up is at nine.

11:55.110 --> 11:58.450
Before then, I have to set
my Landmark in Fifticia,

11:58.450 --> 12:01.700
make it so I can travel
back here from Rabitz,

12:01.700 --> 12:05.580
and have Beelach fix up
my Gilta Brille for me.

12:05.580 --> 12:11.170
It'll be a while with those two,
so I want to take a nap, too.

12:11.170 --> 12:12.340
And then...

12:12.920 --> 12:16.630
I need to stock up
on items and equipment...

12:17.110 --> 12:21.970
Oh, right. I also want to test out
the changes made to my Mark.

12:23.640 --> 12:26.060
I might be short on time.

12:26.060 --> 12:29.980
Still, Emul's transformation
sure is something.

12:29.980 --> 12:32.060
Can you do that too, Ceecrue?

12:33.230 --> 12:34.650
Ceecrue?

12:35.150 --> 12:36.400
Hello?

12:36.400 --> 12:40.110
I-I am a box. Boxes do not speak.

12:40.110 --> 12:41.910
Oh, yeah, right.

12:41.910 --> 12:43.740
So that's supposed to be a box?

12:44.740 --> 12:48.580
Are there any Vorpal Bunnies
who are actually good at camo?

12:52.500 --> 12:55.800
Oh, this place looks quite deserted.

12:55.800 --> 12:59.680
Gotta have the door to Rabitz
in an alley, or else it will stand out.

13:04.390 --> 13:06.470
Acquirer of strength.

13:06.470 --> 13:08.350
That startled me...

13:08.350 --> 13:09.600
Who's this old man?

13:10.770 --> 13:15.360
Allow me to awaken your Arcanum.

13:16.860 --> 13:19.530
A fortune teller NPC?

13:19.530 --> 13:23.120
I give it a ten for atmosphere,
but he won't find any customer here.

13:23.120 --> 13:26.080
Acquirer of strength.

13:26.080 --> 13:30.330
Allow me to awaken your Arcanum.

13:30.330 --> 13:32.040
I heard you the first time.

13:32.710 --> 13:35.380
You sure are talking like
some old-school NPC.

13:35.380 --> 13:39.720
Sunraku, that man is
Arcanoom the Monk of Awakening.

13:39.720 --> 13:40.510
Huh?

13:40.890 --> 13:44.430
If I'm not mistaken,
you just recently hit level 99, right?

13:44.430 --> 13:45.600
Yeah.

13:45.600 --> 13:48.970
MONK OF AWAKENING - ARCANOOM
Arcanoom is an NPC that appears

13:48.970 --> 13:51.140
MONK OF AWAKENING - ARCANOOM
to players after they reach level 99.

13:51.530 --> 13:55.020
He helps you unlock
a special sub-job; Arcanum.

13:55.450 --> 13:56.520
Arcanum?

13:56.520 --> 13:58.530
ARCANUM = MYSTIC
What's that?

13:58.950 --> 14:04.950
Well, jobs in SLF affect how easily
you can learn magic and skills.

14:04.950 --> 14:06.200
If you're a magician,

14:06.200 --> 14:07.450
MAGIC USER = MAGIC
you'll learn magic faster.

14:07.450 --> 14:08.990
MAGIC USER = MAGIC
If you're a twinblade user,

14:08.990 --> 14:10.620
TWINBLADE USER = SKILL TYPE
you'll learn sword

14:10.620 --> 14:11.960
TWINBLADE USER = SKILL TYPE
or fighting move skills faster.

14:12.360 --> 14:13.530
That's the gist of it.

14:13.530 --> 14:15.460
I kind of understand that.

14:15.460 --> 14:18.630
And Arcanum is a somewhat unique job.

14:18.630 --> 14:23.800
It doesn't affect how you learn skills,
but instead affects your stats.

14:23.800 --> 14:26.430
My stats? Like a buff effect?

14:26.430 --> 14:28.430
And not just simple buffs,

14:28.430 --> 14:31.520
BUFF = STRENGTHENING
but it also gives a clear demerit.

14:31.520 --> 14:34.310
Arcanum comes in many different types.

14:34.980 --> 14:37.240
For example, I have the Arcanum "World."

14:37.240 --> 14:39.340
WORLD
For example, I have the Arcanum "World."

14:39.340 --> 14:42.530
WORLD
In exchange for boosting all my stats,

14:42.530 --> 14:47.830
it also doubles the penalties
I receive from my skills or spells.

14:48.240 --> 14:50.300
Boost on all your stats?

14:50.790 --> 14:53.960
Although it comes with downsides,
that sounds really good!

14:53.960 --> 14:56.210
Yes, it suits my build.

14:56.750 --> 14:59.500
Can you pick which Arcanum you want?

14:59.500 --> 15:02.510
No, you won't know what
you will get until you try.

15:02.510 --> 15:04.760
But it is theorized that
it's not picked at random,

15:04.760 --> 15:09.220
but instead, based on some
parameters of the player.

15:09.590 --> 15:10.760
I see.

15:11.350 --> 15:17.480
If it's decided based on my play style,
I wonder what kind of Arcanum will I get.

15:17.980 --> 15:19.230
All right!

15:19.230 --> 15:21.020
Never know until you try.

15:21.900 --> 15:26.360
I'll take on your Arcanum
challenge or whatever!

15:29.320 --> 15:35.620
Acquirer of strength,
allow me to awaken your Arcanum.

15:38.880 --> 15:40.210
Whoa, Sunraku?!

15:40.210 --> 15:41.960
He got covered!

15:41.960 --> 15:43.300
It's all right.

15:43.300 --> 15:45.340
This is just part of the event.

15:52.470 --> 15:53.680
Are these...

15:55.060 --> 15:56.610
Tarot cards?

15:57.190 --> 16:02.230
Now, fate shall decide on your arcanum.

16:02.230 --> 16:03.940
Pick your card.

16:03.940 --> 16:05.990
In stuff like this,

16:05.990 --> 16:09.450
the result you get will mostly be
the same no matter which you pick.

16:17.120 --> 16:18.460
All right, I've decided.

16:19.570 --> 16:22.590
The arcanum that will affect my stats...

16:25.590 --> 16:26.090
...is this one!

16:26.090 --> 16:27.220
FOOL
...is this one!

16:27.220 --> 16:28.630
FOOL

16:30.050 --> 16:31.200
The Fool?

16:32.350 --> 16:35.850
Oh, you never stay in one place.

16:35.850 --> 16:38.310
Do you wander on a goalless journey,

16:38.310 --> 16:41.820
or is it one with a purpose?

16:53.450 --> 16:54.330
Sunraku!

17:03.960 --> 17:04.960
MERCENARY (TWINBLADE)

17:04.960 --> 17:06.340
MERCENARY (TWINBLADE)
ARCANUM (FOOL)

17:07.840 --> 17:08.420
ARCANUM: FOOL
SKILL RECAST TIME CUT IN HALF.

17:08.420 --> 17:09.470
IN EXCHANGE, THE DAMAGE AND EFFECT TIME
FROM STATUS ALIGNMENT IS DOUBLED,

17:09.470 --> 17:10.840
AND HEALING ITEMS WILL HAVE A SUCCESS RATE
It cuts my recast time in half?

17:10.840 --> 17:12.010
It cuts my recast time in half?

17:12.010 --> 17:13.180
This is...

17:13.180 --> 17:16.680
A total jackpot! A win all around!

17:16.680 --> 17:18.850
Hell yeah!

17:18.850 --> 17:19.940
Amazing!

17:19.940 --> 17:25.070
The Fool Arcanum will
aid you in your comeback.

17:25.070 --> 17:27.650
Yeah! Thanks a lot, old man!

17:27.650 --> 17:28.820
But...

17:28.820 --> 17:30.200
Huh? "But"?

17:30.780 --> 17:36.200
You may call upon the
aid of others no longer.

17:37.700 --> 17:44.880
Thus, any illness shall be an even
sharper blade upon your neck.

17:48.300 --> 17:50.590
So he's saying not to get carried away?

17:50.590 --> 17:53.430
Yeah, healing items now have
a chance of not working on me.

17:53.430 --> 17:57.350
And the effects of debuffs are doubled.
It wasn't all good stuff.

17:58.220 --> 18:01.980
But I can take my sweet time
to recover in Inventoria,

18:02.410 --> 18:04.400
and I've got this Mark on me.

18:05.270 --> 18:09.360
Besides, if I just dodge all attacks,
it'll be no problem!

18:09.360 --> 18:12.950
Basically, the Fool was the best
possible pick for me!

18:12.950 --> 18:14.410
Yeah!

18:14.410 --> 18:16.370
He looks pretty carried away to me.

18:16.990 --> 18:18.840
So you did get The Fool. I knew it.

18:18.840 --> 18:20.660
Huh? What?

18:20.660 --> 18:21.660
You knew it?

18:21.660 --> 18:23.120
U-Uh, no, well...

18:23.120 --> 18:29.380
The Fool is one of the few Arcanum that
the acquiring requirement is known.

18:29.380 --> 18:37.430
It is believed that the less time you take
to reach level 99, the easier it is to get.

18:37.430 --> 18:39.310
Oh?

18:39.930 --> 18:42.850
So I was on the quicker side, huh?

18:42.850 --> 18:45.190
Well, I was in kinda of a hurry.

18:45.730 --> 18:47.690
"Quick" isn't half of it.

18:47.690 --> 18:52.190
Hizutome has only been playing
Shangri-La Frontier for a month.

18:52.780 --> 18:55.740
And he's already reached level 99.

18:55.740 --> 18:58.200
By the way, Rei.
Do you know what this is?

19:01.450 --> 19:03.040
Extend?!

19:04.330 --> 19:10.210
Well, this is the point you reach once
you beat a monster above level 100.

19:10.210 --> 19:11.300
It is a step required to unlock the level cap.

19:11.300 --> 19:13.590
LEVEL CAP UNLOCK
It is a step required to unlock the level cap.

19:13.590 --> 19:15.300
I see.

19:15.300 --> 19:16.680
As I suspected.

19:17.970 --> 19:19.600
He's really amazing.

19:19.600 --> 19:23.350
To think he already obtained
the "Extend" descriptor.

19:23.850 --> 19:26.850
As Extend is needed
to unlock the level cap,

19:26.850 --> 19:29.060
I tried to obtain it myself once.

19:29.690 --> 19:36.280
But that time I had help from
other level-99 Schwarz Vulf members.

19:36.280 --> 19:38.700
That's how difficult it usually is.

19:39.700 --> 19:41.700
But... I should've known.

19:41.700 --> 19:44.620
The Fool fits you perfectly, Mr. Sunraku!

19:44.620 --> 19:48.370
Do you mean to say I'm an idiot, huh?

19:48.370 --> 19:52.210
- I've tried and given up many difficult games
- A half-naked fool! It just writes itself!

19:52.630 --> 19:58.050
but Hizutome beat all of those
and made it look easy.

19:58.050 --> 20:00.640
If someone like him picked up SLF,

20:00.640 --> 20:03.430
not only he would beat
Wethermon the Tombguard before long,

20:03.430 --> 20:08.100
but he also took on that shadow wolf,
even if it was just a fake,

20:08.100 --> 20:11.920
the Lycagon the Nightslayer Schwarz
Vulf has spent a year chasing after,

20:11.920 --> 20:16.450
in just one night, and beat her
without any preparation.

20:17.240 --> 20:19.450
It's more expected than
surprising at this point.

20:20.700 --> 20:22.240
But still...

20:23.080 --> 20:25.580
Not only did we beat an area together,

20:25.580 --> 20:28.210
but I got to be part of that big moment!

20:28.210 --> 20:30.790
What a deep, dense night this was!

20:31.590 --> 20:35.460
A night! We actually spent a night
and saw the sunrise together!

20:35.460 --> 20:39.680
A sudden development!
Maybe I made too much progress?

20:45.610 --> 20:48.770
Well then, that was a pretty
sweet surprise finding,

20:48.770 --> 20:50.850
but it's time to visit Rabitz.

20:51.480 --> 20:55.860
I gotta finish what I need to do
and meet up with Rust and Mordo.

20:55.860 --> 20:58.570
I can't let myself miss out
on the information

20:58.570 --> 21:03.910
on the Unique Monster
Ctarnidd the Abyss those two got.

21:06.700 --> 21:09.460
Do we have to get here this early?

21:09.460 --> 21:11.460
It's still six in the morning.

21:11.830 --> 21:13.500
It's my first login in six months.

21:14.130 --> 21:16.170
I'm sure my senses here got rusty.

21:16.640 --> 21:20.220
You were all about Nephilim
this whole time, after all.

21:20.220 --> 21:23.470
You were too excited about this
SLF robot to sleep, weren't you?

21:23.470 --> 21:24.930
- Shut up!
- Ouch!

21:25.640 --> 21:28.600
Quit spouting nonsense
and get going, Mordo.

21:29.100 --> 21:30.730
MORDO

21:30.730 --> 21:32.850
MORDO
Got it, Rust.

21:35.610 --> 21:39.360
RUST

22:06.890 --> 22:11.890
NEW CHAPTER "THE SKY ABOVE,
THE SPREAD-OUT SEA, BEYOND THE ABYSSAL CITY"
